### Task 1 – Hello World

* Print `Hello World`.

* Print your name, course name and institute name.

### Task 2 – Variables & Data Types

Declare and print the following variables using appropriate data types:

* Name – String

* Age – int

* Mark – float

* Height – double

* Gender – char

* Is Student – boolean

* Mobile Number – long

* Grade – char

* Total Fees – double

* Number of Subjects – byte

### Task 3 – Byte Data Type

* Declare a variable using `byte`.

* Assign a value and print it.

* Check the minimum and maximum values of byte.

* Try assigning a value outside the byte range and observe the error.

### Task 4 – Java Data Types

Declare and display all 8 primitive data types:

* byte

* short

* int

* long

* float

* double

* char

* boolean

### Task 5 – Operators in Java

1\. Arithmetic Operators

* Addition (+)

* Subtraction (-)

* Multiplication (\*)

* Division (/)

* Modulus (%)

2\. Assignment Operators

* Assignment (=)

* Addition assignment (+=)

* Subtraction assignment (-=)

* Multiplication assignment (\*=)

* Division assignment (/=)

* Modulus assignment (%=)

3\. Conditional Operator

* Find the biggest of two numbers using the ternary operator.

* Check whether a number is even or odd.

4\. Unary Operators

* Pre-increment (++a)

* Post-increment (a++)

* Pre-decrement (--a)

* Post-decrement (a--)

5\. Logical Operators

* AND (&&)

* OR (||)

* NOT (!)
